$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Wave-induced set-up on a sloping beach, two-dimensional
$ Domain: 2 km x 1 km, depth from 10 m in the west to 0.5 m in the east;
$ waves and wind from the west-south-west.
$ In a two-dimensional run SETUPP solves a Poisson equation for the
$ water level in SETUP2D. No other registered case uses SETUP.
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'SETUP' '2D'
SET NAUTICAL
MODE STATIONARY TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

$ Computational grid: 40 x 20 meshes of 50 m.
$ Spectral grid: 36 directions and 24 frequencies from 0.05 to 1.0 Hz.
CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 2000.0 1000.0 40 20 CIRCLE 36 0.05 1.0 24
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 40 20 50.0 50.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'slope.bot' 3 0 FREE

WIND 10.0 250.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 1.5 8.0 250.0 20.0

$ Keep the physics explicit so changes to defaults do not alter the case.
GEN3 KOMEN
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038
SETUP
NUMERIC STOPC 0.001 0.01 0.001 99.5 STAT 30

BLOCK 'COMPGRID' NOHEADER 'setup2d.blk' LAYOUT 3 HSIGN SETUP
POINTS 'LINE' 1000. 500. 1500. 500. 1800. 500. 1900. 300.
TABLE 'LINE' HEADER 'setup2d.tbl' XP YP DEPTH HSIGN SETUP TM01 DIR

COMPUTE
STOP
